\begin{abstract}
This dissertation presents a unified Hamiltonian framework capable of evolving 
general relativity, quantum mechanics, electromagnetism, magnetohydrodynamics, 
and nuclear physics within a single mathematically continuous operator. 
The resulting Master Hamiltonian integrates explicit cross-domain coupling terms, 
including gravitational wave--quantum mechanical interactions and electromagnetic--nuclear 
feedback. The framework is evaluated through astrophysical validation tests, 
cryptographic verification layers, and Planck-scale lattice simulations. 
The work establishes a foundation for unified cosmological computation.
\end{abstract}

\chapter{Introduction}
The goal of unified cosmology is to construct a single Hamiltonian operator 
that governs the evolution of all major physical domains. Traditional physics 
engines treat these domains independently. This dissertation introduces a 
cross-coupled Hamiltonian formalism capable of evolving the universe as a 
single coherent physical object.

